    "q-81263": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81263",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}u\\operatorname{ln}⁡v \\\\ {u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have $x=u\\operatorname{ln}⁡v$ and $y={u}^{2}{v}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\frac{u}{v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u{v}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2{u}^{2}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡v & \\frac{u}{v} \\\\ 2u{v}^{2} & 2{u}^{2}v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡v\\cdot 2{u}^{2}v-\\frac{u}{v}\\cdot 2u{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡v-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
